eye-contact-co-processing-at-the-speed-of-light-lines-5 : List (List Word)
eye-contact-co-processing-at-the-speed-of-light-lines-5 = cons "The Speed of Light: Minimum Achievable Latency" (cons "From special relativity: information cannot propagate faster than the speed of light (c ≈ 300,000 km/s in vacuum). This isn't a technological limitation—it's fundamental structure of causality itself. Your light cone defines what can influence you and what you can influence." (cons "Light in air travels slightly slower (~99.97% of c) but this is negligibly close to the physical minimum. When photons travel from one person's face to another person's retina 2 meters away:" (cons "Transit time: ~6.7 nanoseconds" (cons "This is as fast as physics allows for spatially separated systems to exchange information. There is no faster coupling possible while maintaining distinct boundaries." (cons "Compare to neural transmission:" (cons "Action potentials in neurons: ~0.5-120 m/s (depending on myelination)" (cons "Light in air: ~300,000,000 m/s" (cons "Light is ~6 million times faster than fastest neural signals" (cons "The photon exchange between faces happens effectively instantaneously on the timescale of neural processing. By the time your neurons fire in response to seeing their face, the electromagnetic information has already traversed the space thousands of times over." nil)))))))))
